{"unit_slug":"barbarian_rage","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["activate","class_feature_root","grant_extra_action","rest_window","use_count"],"harness_relations":["consumes","grants","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"atom_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_atom","name":"grant_resistance","justification":"Rage grants Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage while active. No resistance-granting effect atom exists in ClassFeatureEffect or anywhere in the surface.","evidence":"Damage Resistance. You have Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"grant_damage_bonus","justification":"Rage grants a flat bonus to damage rolls on Strength-based weapon and Unarmed Strike attacks. This bonus scales by class level (threshold_tiers). No effect atom models a conditional damage bonus keyed on the attack's ability score.","evidence":"Rage Damage. When you make an attack using Strength — with either a weapon or an Unarmed Strike — and deal damage to the target, you gain a bonus to the damage that increases as you gain levels as a Barbarian."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"grant_stat_advantage","justification":"Rage grants Advantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws. The existing modify_roll_advantage atom is a mastery rider (on-hit, per-target); it does not model a blanket always-active advantage on a specific ability's checks and saves.","evidence":"Strength Advantage. You have Advantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"prohibit_spellcasting","justification":"Rage prevents casting spells and maintaining Concentration while active. The surface has no 'restrict_spellcasting' or 'drop_concentration' effect atom. restrict_action_set only covers StandardActionKind; casting spells and holding concentration are not a StandardActionKind.","evidence":"No Concentration or Spells. You can't maintain Concentration, and you can't cast spells."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"class_feature_ongoing_state","justification":"Rage is not a one-shot activation (ClassFeatureActivationMechanics). It enters a persistent state that lasts until the end of the barbarian's next turn, extended each turn by specific actions (attack, force save, bonus action). ClassFeatureActivationMechanics has no 'duration' field and no renewal-condition grammar. A new family (e.g. 'ongoing_state') or a duration+renewal extension to 'activation' is required.","evidence":"Duration. The Rage lasts until the end of your next turn, and it ends early if you don Heavy armor or have the Incapacitated condition. If your Rage is still active on your next turn, you can extend the Rage for another round by doing one of the following: Make an attack roll against an enemy. Force an enemy to make a saving throw. Take a Bonus Action to extend your Rage."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"early_end_condition","justification":"Rage ends early on two state-based triggers: donning Heavy armor or gaining the Incapacitated condition. No surface atom models state-based early-termination conditions on a class feature's active state.","evidence":"it ends early if you don Heavy armor or have the Incapacitated condition"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["claude claimed atom 'bonus_action_quota' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'scale_numeric_bonus' not in tracer output"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":2.164}

{"unit_slug":"fire_bolt","verdict":"surface_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["action_quota","activate","attack_roll","damage","on_hit_window","scale_die_count","spell_root","target"],"harness_relations":["attaches_to","consumes","grants","modifies","opens_window","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"surface_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_variant","name":"ignite_object","justification":"Fire Bolt ignites flammable unattended objects on hit. The current Effect union only has `damage` and `none`; there is no variant for object-state environmental effects. Encoding this rule requires a new Effect variant that marks an object as burning.","evidence":"A flammable object hit by this spell starts burning if it isn't being worn or carried."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":2.262}

{"unit_slug":"paladin_lay_on_hands","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["activate","class_feature_root","grant_extra_action","rest_window","use_count"],"harness_relations":["consumes","grants","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"atom_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_atom","name":"hp_pool","justification":"Lay On Hands tracks a continuous HP budget (not discrete uses) that is partially expendable per activation. The current use_count atom implies discrete tokens; here the resource is a pool of HP points that scales as 5 × paladin level and can be drawn in any amount per activation (1 HP to remaining max). Multiple activations can draw from the same pool until exhausted. This is fundamentally different from use_count and cannot be expressed with any existing UseCountCap variant.","evidence":"You have a pool of healing power that replenishes when you finish a Long Rest. With that pool, you can restore a total number of Hit Points equal to five times your Paladin level."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"remove_condition","justification":"A new ClassFeatureEffect variant is needed to represent removing a condition from a target creature. This is distinct from apply_condition (which exists in mastery effects) and from heal_hp. The Poisoned removal costs 5 HP from the pool but does NOT restore HP — so it is not a heal variant either.","evidence":"You can also expend 5 Hit Points from the pool of healing power to remove the Poisoned condition from the creature; those points don't also restore Hit Points to the creature."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"branched_effect_choice","justification":"The unit offers two distinct activation modes (heal HP, or remove Poisoned for 5 HP) as an either/or player choice within a single Bonus Action use. ClassFeatureActivationMechanics carries a single effect field; there is no branched-choice shape to represent this. A new variant or a multi-effect composition shape is needed.","evidence":"As a Bonus Action, you can touch a creature and draw power from the pool ... You can also expend 5 Hit Points from the pool of healing power to remove the Poisoned condition."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["claude claimed atom 'bonus_action_quota' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'heal' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'scale_numeric_bonus' not in tracer output","tracer emitted atom 'grant_extra_action' not in claude's claim"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.83}

{"unit_slug":"rogue_sneak_attack","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["activate","class_feature_root","grant_extra_action","rest_window","use_count"],"harness_relations":["consumes","grants","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"class_feature_passive_on_hit_rider","justification":"Sneak Attack is a passive conditional on-hit damage rider that fires automatically when attack conditions are met, not an explicit activation. The `ClassFeatureActivationMechanics` family requires player-initiated activation and a rest-based use-count reset. A new payload family composing on_hit_window + damage + use_count/turn_start_window + conditional gate is needed.","evidence":"Once per turn, you can deal an extra 1d6 damage to one creature you hit with an attack roll if you have Advantage on the roll and the attack uses a Finesse or a Ranged weapon."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"per_turn (RestResetCadence)","justification":"Sneak Attack's use-count resets at the start of each turn, not on a short or long rest. `RestResetCadence` only supports rest-based resets (short_or_long_rest, long_rest, short_rest, partial_short_full_long). A turn-based reset variant connecting use_count to turn_start_window is required.","evidence":"Once per turn, you can deal an extra 1d6 damage..."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"conditional_prerequisite_gate (advantage_or_ally_adjacency)","justification":"The feature fires only when: (a) the rogue has Advantage on the attack roll, OR (b) an ally is within 5 feet of the target AND that ally is not Incapacitated AND the rogue does not have Disadvantage. This compound condition check has no atom in v4 taxonomy. The `requires` relation exists but there is no predicate atom for advantage state or ally positioning.","evidence":"if you have Advantage on the roll... You don't need Advantage on the attack roll if at least one of your allies is within 5 feet of the target, the ally doesn't have the Incapacitated condition, and you don't have Disadvantage on the attack roll."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"weapon_passthrough (DamageType)","justification":"The extra damage has the same type as the weapon's damage type. DamageType is a closed 13-value enum (acid, bludgeoning, cold, ...). There is no 'weapon' or 'same_as_weapon' passthrough variant. Encoding it as any fixed type would be incorrect.","evidence":"The extra damage's type is the same as the weapon's type."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"weapon_property_filter (finesse_or_ranged)","justification":"The on-hit trigger only applies when the attack uses a weapon with the Finesse or Ranged property. No weapon property filter exists for class feature mechanics (or for on_hit_window in general). The mastery trigger has 'weapon_hit' and 'weapon_hit_melee_only' but no Finesse/Ranged variant.","evidence":"the attack uses a Finesse or a Ranged weapon"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["claude claimed atom 'heal' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'scale_die_count' not in tracer output","tracer emitted atom 'grant_extra_action' not in claude's claim"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":2.053}


{"unit_slug":"monk_focus_points","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["activate","class_feature_root","grant_extra_action","rest_window","scale_numeric_bonus","use_count"],"harness_relations":["consumes","grants","modifies","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"resource_pool_family","justification":"Focus Points is not a single activation — it is a shared resource pool consumed by multiple sub-features (Flurry of Blows, Patient Defense, Step of the Wind). The current 'activation' family forces a single effect per record and cannot model a pool that multiple distinct activations draw from. A new 'resource_pool' family is needed: it would carry the pool size (with level scaling) and reset cadence, without requiring an attached effect — the consumers reference it by id.","evidence":"You can expend these points to enhance or fuel certain Monk features. You start knowing three such features: Flurry of Blows, Patient Defense, and Step of the Wind"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"grant_unarmed_strikes","justification":"Flurry of Blows grants two Unarmed Strikes specifically. The existing 'grant_extra_action' atom models one extra standard action with an optional exclusion list — it cannot represent 'two Unarmed Strikes' (a specific attack type, not a generic action).","evidence":"You can expend 1 Focus Point to make two Unarmed Strikes as a Bonus Action."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"grant_standard_action_bundle","justification":"Patient Defense and Step of the Wind each grant a specific pair of standard actions (Disengage+Dodge and Disengage+Dash respectively) as a single bonus action expenditure. The current 'grant_extra_action' can grant one extra action with restrictions, but cannot model 'grant two specific actions simultaneously as one bonus action'.","evidence":"you can expend 1 Focus Point to take both the Disengage and the Dodge actions as a Bonus Action."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"modify_jump_distance","justification":"Step of the Wind's focus-spending mode doubles jump distance for the turn. There is no movement-modifier effect atom in the current vocabulary.","evidence":"your jump distance is doubled for the turn."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"UseCountCap.linear_per_level","justification":"Focus Points = Monk Level (L2=2, L3=3, …, L20=20), a perfectly linear per-level scale. UseCountCap only supports 'fixed' or 'threshold_tiers'. Without a 'linear_per_level' variant, the 1-point-per-level progression must be expressed as 18 explicit tier entries — verbose and not semantically distinct from a true threshold pattern. This is a surface_widening within the scaling vocabulary.","evidence":"Your Monk level determines the number of points you have, as shown in the Focus Points column of the Monk Features table. [Table: L2=2, L3=3, …, L20=20]"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.958}

{"unit_slug":"eldritch_blast","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["action_quota","activate","attack_roll","damage","on_hit_window","spell_root","target"],"harness_relations":["attaches_to","consumes","grants","opens_window","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_variant","name":"attack_roll_phase.count","justification":"Eldritch Blast's cantrip upgrade fires N separate attack rolls per cast, where N scales by character level (1@L1-4, 2@L5-10, 3@L11-16, 4@L17+). The current 'attack_roll' ActivationPhase has no 'count' field — it is always exactly one attack roll per phase entry. Adding an optional 'count: ThresholdTiers<number>' with axis='character' to the attack_roll phase variant would express this directly and cleanly.","evidence":"The spell creates two beams at level 5, three beams at level 11, and four beams at level 17. You can direct the beams at the same target or at different ones. Make a separate attack roll for each beam."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"Attachment.target.selection: mode 'repeated'","justification":"Alternatively, the TargetSelection union needs a 'repeated' mode (as distinct from 'choose_up_to') to express 'N independent attack roll instances, each against any target in range, where N is a character-level threshold-tiered count'. The existing 'choose_up_to' with SlotScaling only handles slot-level linear multi-target selection for a single resolution, not N separate resolutions.","evidence":"Make a separate attack roll for each beam. [beams = 2 at L5, 3 at L11, 4 at L17]"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.825}

{"unit_slug":"shillelagh","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["activate","bonus_action_quota","expire","modify_roll_numeric","persist","spell_root","target"],"harness_relations":["attaches_to","consumes","grants","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"atom_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_variant","name":"Attachment::weapon","justification":"Shillelagh imbues a weapon the caster is holding, not the caster themselves. The `weapon` attachment atom exists in v4 taxonomy (§3) but is absent from the `Attachment` union in types.ts. The `self` attachment used in the approximation misrepresents the binding site: the effect is on the weapon, not the caster's body.","evidence":"A Club or Quarterstaff you are holding is imbued with nature's power."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"OngoingOperation::modify_roll_substitute","justification":"The `modify_roll_substitute` effect atom exists in v4 taxonomy (§9 effect atoms) but has no corresponding variant in `OngoingOperation` (types.ts only has `roll_modifier` and `damage_on_hit`). Shillelagh's core benefit is substituting the ability modifier used for attack and damage rolls (WIS/CHA spellcasting ability in place of STR). This cannot be expressed as a `roll_modifier` delta — the substitution replaces the base modifier entirely rather than adding to it.","evidence":"you can use your spellcasting ability instead of Strength for the attack and damage rolls of melee attacks using that weapon"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"damage_type_choice","justification":"No v4 atom represents a per-hit caster choice between two damage types. The `damage` effect atom takes a fixed `damageType`. Shillelagh allows the caster to choose on each hit whether damage is Force or the weapon's normal damage type. This is distinct from both fixed damage typing and damage resistance bypass. A new atom (or a new variant of `damage`) is needed to model a closed set of selectable damage types.","evidence":"If the attack deals damage, it can be Force damage or the weapon's normal damage type (your choice)."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"Lifecycle::replace_on_recast","justification":"The `replace_on_recast` lifecycle atom exists in v4 taxonomy (§6 lifecycle atoms) but is not handled by the tracer. Shillelagh explicitly ends if the caster re-casts it — a replace-on-recast semantics distinct from normal `persist`/`expire`. The `let go of the weapon` termination is a separate condition (weapon-release expiry) also unrepresented.","evidence":"The spell ends early if you cast it again or if you let go of the weapon."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["claude claimed atom 'damage' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'on_hit_window' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'scale_die_size' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'self' not in tracer output","tracer emitted atom 'modify_roll_numeric' not in claude's claim","tracer emitted atom 'target' not in claude's claim"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.865}

{"unit_slug":"magic_missile","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["action_quota","activate","attack_roll","damage","on_hit_window","scale_target_count","spell_root","spell_slot","target"],"harness_relations":["attaches_to","consumes","grants","modifies","opens_window","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"atom_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_atom","name":"forced_apply","justification":"Magic Missile darts hit unconditionally — no attack roll, no saving throw. The v4 resolution atoms (attack_roll, save_gate, interrupt_resolution) all gate effects behind a dice resolution. A new resolution atom is needed to express 'damage is delivered to the target with no roll' so the graph correctly omits the on_hit_window.","evidence":"Each dart strikes a creature of your choice that you can see within range. A dart deals 1d4+1 Force damage to its target."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"ActivationPhase::auto_damage","justification":"ActivationPhase is a discriminated union of {attack_roll, save_gate}. Neither branch fits a guaranteed-hit delivery. A new variant { kind: 'auto_damage'; attachment: Attachment; effect: Effect } is needed to surface the forced_apply atom and remove the false on_hit_window from the graph.","evidence":"The darts all strike simultaneously, and you can direct them to hit one creature or several."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.422}

{"unit_slug":"shield","verdict":"clean","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["commit","expire","interrupt_resolution","modify_ac","negate_named_effect","persist","prepare","prompt","reaction_quota","reaction_window","respond","self","spell_root","spell_slot"],"harness_relations":["attaches_to","commits","consumes","grants","opens_window","persists_until","prepares","prompts","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"clean","claude_proposed_widenings":[],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.562}

{"unit_slug":"hunters_mark","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["activate","bonus_action_quota","concentrate","concentration_lock","damage","expire","mark","mark_target","on_hit_window","spell_root","spell_slot","transfer_mark"],"harness_relations":["attaches_to","consumes","grants","opens_window","persists_until","roots","transfers_to"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"atom_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_atom","name":"advantage_on_check","justification":"Hunter's Mark grants Advantage on Wisdom (Perception or Survival) checks to locate the marked target. The current OngoingOperation union has no variant for advantage/disadvantage on skill checks. RollKind = 'attack_roll' | 'saving_throw' — skill checks are outside the closed enum. No atom in the v4 vocabulary covers this.","evidence":"You also have Advantage on any Wisdom (Perception or Survival) check you make to find it."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"OngoingEffectMechanics.operations (plural)","justification":"OngoingEffectMechanics.operation is a singular field. Hunter's Mark has TWO simultaneous ongoing effects: damage_on_hit and advantage_on_check. With a singular operation field, only one effect can be encoded. The field needs to become ReadonlyArray<OngoingOperation> to accommodate multi-effect ongoing spells.","evidence":"you deal an extra 1d6 Force damage to the target whenever you hit it with an attack roll. You also have Advantage on any Wisdom (Perception or Survival) check you make to find it."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"Duration slot-scaling","justification":"At higher spell slots the concentration duration extends: slot 3-4 → 8 hours, slot 5+ → 24 hours. The Duration type only supports a fixed DurationValue; there is no slot-scaling variant. This is a surface_widening (new Duration variant) rather than a new atom, but it is needed for a faithful upcast encoding.","evidence":"Your Concentration can last longer with a spell slot of level 3-4 (up to 8 hours) or 5+ (up to 24 hours)."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.75}

{"unit_slug":"alarm","verdict":"clean","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["action_quota","area","expire","persist","post_action_window","release","spell_root","spell_slot","store"],"harness_relations":["attaches_to","consumes","grants","opens_window","persists_until","prompts","roots","stores"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"clean","claude_proposed_widenings":[],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.851}

{"unit_slug":"fireball","verdict":"refused","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"refused","claude_proposed_widenings":[],"claude_confidence":"low","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3533147-fireball/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:1733\n      throw new Error(`unhandled dice amount: ${String(_exhaustive)}`);\n            ^\n\n\nError: unhandled dice amount: [object Object]\n    at describeDiceAmount (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3533147-fireball/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:1733:13)\n    at traceEffect (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3533147-fireball/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:1018:27)\n    at traceSaveBranch (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3533147-fireball/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:880:15)\n    at tracePhase (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3533147-fireball/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:844:7)\n    at <anonymous> (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3533147-fireball/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:767:30)\n    at Array.forEach (<anonymous>)\n    at traceActivation (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3533147-fireball/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:766:12)\n    at traceSpellMechanics (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3533147-fireball/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:166:7)\n    at traceSpellUnit (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3533147-fireball/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:118:23)\n    at traceUnit (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3533147-fireball/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:83:14)\n\nNode.js v20.20.1\n","wall_seconds":2.062}

{"unit_slug":"counterspell","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"surface_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"target":"ReactionTrigger","variant":"creature_casting_spell","shape":"{ kind: \"creature_casting_spell\" }","v4_atom":"spell_cast_window","rationale":"Counterspell triggers when any creature within 60 ft begins casting a spell. The existing trigger variants only cover hit_by_attack_roll and targeted_by_named_spell (both Shield-shaped). Counterspell needs a generic open-world trigger variant — the caster is not a named spell. Maps to v4 atom spell_cast_window (Window §4)."},{"target":"ReactionEffect","variant":"save_gated_negate_current_spell","shape":"{ kind: \"save_gated_negate_current_spell\"; ability: Ability; dc: DcSource }","v4_atoms":["save_gate","negate_named_effect","refunds"],"rationale":"Counterspell's effect is: target makes a CON save; on failure, the spell being cast is negated (slot refunded). The existing negate_named_effect requires a specific spellId at encoding time, but Counterspell negates whatever is currently being cast (unknown statically). A bundled variant captures the save gate + open-world negation + slot-refund semantics in one effect node. All three underlying v4 atoms (save_gate, negate_named_effect, refunds) already exist in the taxonomy."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["claude claimed atom 'respond' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'reaction_window' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'spell_cast_window' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'save_gate' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'negate_named_effect' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'refunds' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'target' not in tracer output"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3574349-counterspell/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:276\n      throw new Error(`unhandled reaction trigger: ${String(_)}`);\n            ^\n\n\nError: unhandled reaction trigger: [object Object]\n    at describeReactionTrigger (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3574349-counterspell/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:276:13)\n    at traceTriggeredReaction (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3574349-counterspell/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:531:9)\n    at traceSpellMechanics (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3574349-counterspell/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:169:7)\n    at traceSpellUnit (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3574349-counterspell/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:118:23)\n    at traceUnit (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3574349-counterspell/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:83:14)\n    at main (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3574349-counterspell/src/run.ts:31:17)\n    at <anonymous> (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3574349-counterspell/src/run.ts:49:1)\n    at ModuleJob.run (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:325:25)\n    at async ModuleLoader.import (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:606:24)\n    at async asyncRunEntryPointWithESMLoader (node:internal/modules/run_main:117:5)\n\nNode.js v20.20.1\n","wall_seconds":1.872}

{"unit_slug":"polymorph","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["action_quota","activate","concentrate","concentration_lock","expire","save_gate","spell_root","spell_slot","target"],"harness_relations":["attaches_to","consumes","grants","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"atom_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_atom","name":"transform_creature","justification":"Polymorph's on-fail effect replaces the target's stat block with a chosen Beast's stat block while the concentration persists. This is a distinct effect category — it is not damage, a roll modifier, a mark, an AC change, or a negation. The surface has no effect atom that represents a creature undergoing a form change that overrides its statistics for the duration.","evidence":"The target's game statistics are replaced by the stat block of the chosen Beast, but the target retains its alignment, personality, creature type, Hit Points, and Hit Point Dice."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"grant_temp_hp","justification":"The spell grants Temporary Hit Points equal to the Beast form's HP at the moment of transformation. No such effect atom exists in v4. The existing heal_hp atom (class-feature family) restores current HP; Temporary HP are a separate resource bucket with distinct rules (SRD §Temporary Hit Points). A new effect atom is needed that specifically grants Temp HP, with the amount sourced from the chosen Beast form rather than a fixed DiceExpr.","evidence":"The target gains a number of Temporary Hit Points equal to the Hit Points of the Beast form."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"temp_hp_depleted_ends_concentration","justification":"The spell has a bespoke early-termination condition: it ends when the target has no Temporary Hit Points remaining. This is structurally different from the standard concentration-drop lifecycle (creature fails a concentration check, loses concentration, or drops the spell voluntarily). The existing concentrate → expire subgraph only models time-based expiry. A lifecycle atom is needed for 'resource-depleted → concentration ends' that can hook onto the Temp HP pool granted by grant_temp_hp.","evidence":"The spell ends early on the target if it has no Temporary Hit Points left."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.868}

{"unit_slug":"protection_from_energy","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"atom_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_variant","name":"damage_resistance","justification":"The spell's entire mechanic is granting Resistance (halving incoming damage of the chosen type) to the touched creature. The existing OngoingOperation union only covers roll_modifier (adds dice to attack/save rolls) and damage_on_hit (adds damage when caster hits the target). Neither can encode 'halve incoming damage of type X'. A new variant is required.","evidence":"the willing creature you touch has Resistance to one damage type of your choice: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"caster_choice_damage_type","justification":"The damage type is not fixed at authoring time — it is chosen by the caster at the moment of casting from a closed enumerated list. All existing damage type references in the surface are fixed DamageType string literals. A caster_choice variant with a 'from' field (closed list of DamageType values) is needed to capture this pattern accurately.","evidence":"one damage type of your choice: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["claude claimed atom 'spell_root' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'activate' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'action_quota' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'spell_slot' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'concentration_lock' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'concentrate' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'expire' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'target' not in tracer output"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3689541-protection_from_energy/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:509\n      throw new Error(`unhandled ongoing operation: ${String(_)}`);\n            ^\n\n\nError: unhandled ongoing operation: [object Object]\n    at traceOngoingOperation (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3689541-protection_from_energy/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:509:13)\n    at traceOngoingEffect (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3689541-protection_from_energy/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:382:3)\n    at traceSpellMechanics (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3689541-protection_from_energy/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:163:7)\n    at traceSpellUnit (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3689541-protection_from_energy/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:118:23)\n    at traceUnit (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3689541-protection_from_energy/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:83:14)\n    at main (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3689541-protection_from_energy/src/run.ts:31:17)\n    at <anonymous> (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3689541-protection_from_energy/src/run.ts:49:1)\n    at ModuleJob.run (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:325:25)\n    at async ModuleLoader.import (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:606:24)\n    at async asyncRunEntryPointWithESMLoader (node:internal/modules/run_main:117:5)\n\nNode.js v20.20.1\n","wall_seconds":1.9}

{"unit_slug":"fighter_action_surge","verdict":"surface_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["activate","class_feature_root","grant_extra_action","rest_window","restrict_action_set","use_count"],"harness_relations":["consumes","grants","modifies","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"surface_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_variant","name":"ClassFeatureUsageLimit (once_per_turn)","justification":"At level 17, Action Surge grants 2 uses per rest but only 1 per turn. ClassFeatureActivationMechanics has no usageLimit field. The concept already exists in MasteryUsageLimit { kind: 'once_per_turn' } but is not wired to the class feature domain. A new optional usageLimit field on ClassFeatureActivationMechanics — reusing or mirroring MasteryUsageLimit — would capture this constraint.","evidence":"Starting at level 17, you can use it twice before a rest but only once on a turn."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["claude claimed atom 'scale_numeric_bonus' not in tracer output"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":2.304}

