{"unit_slug":"death_ward","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"atom_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[],"claude_confidence":null,"discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3672865-death_ward/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:509\n      throw new Error(`unhandled ongoing operation: ${String(_)}`);\n            ^\n\n\nError: unhandled ongoing operation: [object Object]\n    at traceOngoingOperation (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3672865-death_ward/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:509:13)\n    at traceOngoingEffect (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3672865-death_ward/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:382:3)\n    at traceSpellMechanics (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3672865-death_ward/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:163:7)\n    at traceSpellUnit (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3672865-death_ward/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:118:23)\n    at traceUnit (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3672865-death_ward/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:83:14)\n    at main (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3672865-death_ward/src/run.ts:31:17)\n    at <anonymous> (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3672865-death_ward/src/run.ts:49:1)\n    at ModuleJob.run (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:325:25)\n    at async ModuleLoader.import (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:606:24)\n    at async asyncRunEntryPointWithESMLoader (node:internal/modules/run_main:117:5)\n\nNode.js v20.20.1\n","wall_seconds":1.502}

{"unit_slug":"bard_bardic_inspiration","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["activate","class_feature_root","grant_extra_action","rest_window","use_count"],"harness_relations":["consumes","grants","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"atom_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_atom","name":"reroll_saving_throw","justification":"The core mechanic of Indomitable is rerolling a failed saving throw. There is no effect variant in ClassFeatureEffect for rerolling a die roll. Neither grant_extra_action nor heal_hp approximates this.","evidence":"If you fail a saving throw, you can reroll it with a bonus equal to your Fighter level."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"ClassFeatureActivationCost.on_failed_save","justification":"Indomitable fires reactively after a failed saving throw, not proactively on the character's turn. The existing activation cost variants (free, bonus_action) model proactive turn-based activation only. A trigger variant is needed to model the 'when you fail a saving throw' condition.","evidence":"If you fail a saving throw, you can reroll it..."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"FlatBonusSource.class_level","justification":"The reroll bonus equals the character's Fighter level — a flat integer derived from class level, not a dice expression. There is no bonus-source concept in the surface that produces a flat bonus equal to class level. The existing DiceAmount / DiceExprDelta types model additive dice deltas and fixed flat integers, not dynamic class-level-derived integers.","evidence":"...you can reroll it with a bonus equal to your Fighter level."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.704}

{"unit_slug":"fighter_indomitable","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"atom_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_atom","name":"reroll_saving_throw","justification":"The core mechanic of Indomitable is rerolling a failed saving throw. There is no effect variant in ClassFeatureEffect for rerolling a die roll. Neither grant_extra_action nor heal_hp approximates this.","evidence":"If you fail a saving throw, you can reroll it with a bonus equal to your Fighter level."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"ClassFeatureActivationCost.on_failed_save","justification":"Indomitable fires reactively after a failed saving throw, not proactively on the character's turn. The existing activation cost variants (free, bonus_action) model proactive turn-based activation only. A trigger variant is needed to model the 'when you fail a saving throw' condition.","evidence":"If you fail a saving throw, you can reroll it..."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"FlatBonusSource.class_level","justification":"The reroll bonus equals the character's Fighter level — a flat integer derived from class level, not a dice expression. There is no bonus-source concept in the surface that produces a flat bonus equal to class level. The existing DiceAmount / DiceExprDelta types model additive dice deltas and fixed flat integers, not dynamic class-level-derived integers.","evidence":"...you can reroll it with a bonus equal to your Fighter level."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3977122-fighter_indomitable/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:1371\n      throw new Error(`unhandled class-feature effect: ${String(_exhaustive)}`);\n            ^\n\n\nError: unhandled class-feature effect: [object Object]\n    at traceClassFeatureEffect (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3977122-fighter_indomitable/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:1371:13)\n    at traceClassFeatureActivation (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3977122-fighter_indomitable/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:1208:3)\n    at traceClassFeatureMechanics (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3977122-fighter_indomitable/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:1177:14)\n    at traceClassFeatureUnit (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3977122-fighter_indomitable/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:1152:23)\n    at traceUnit (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3977122-fighter_indomitable/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:85:14)\n    at main (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3977122-fighter_indomitable/src/run.ts:31:17)\n    at <anonymous> (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3977122-fighter_indomitable/src/run.ts:49:1)\n    at ModuleJob.run (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:325:25)\n    at async ModuleLoader.import (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:606:24)\n    at async asyncRunEntryPointWithESMLoader (node:internal/modules/run_main:117:5)\n\nNode.js v20.20.1\n","wall_seconds":2.046}

{"unit_slug":"fighter_extra_attack","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"ClassFeaturePassiveMechanics (passive_modifier family)","justification":"Extra Attack has no activation cost, no use count, and no rest reset cadence — it is always-on from the moment it is acquired. The only existing class-feature family is 'activation' (ClassFeatureActivationMechanics), which requires activationCost, resource, and resetCadence. These fields have no valid instantiation for Extra Attack: there is no use count (unlimited), no reset cadence (permanent), and no activation (implicit within the Attack action). A new family — 'passive_modifier' — is required for always-on class features that do not consume a resource.","evidence":"You can attack twice instead of once whenever you take the Attack action on your turn."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"modify_attack_count (ClassFeatureEffect variant)","justification":"The mechanic sets the number of attacks available within a single Attack action. The existing ClassFeatureEffect variants are grant_extra_action (grants a full additional action, e.g. Action Surge) and heal_hp. Neither models 'when you take the Attack action, you make N attacks instead of 1'. The v4 taxonomy (TAXONOMY_atoms_graph.md) names scale_attack_count as the scaling atom for this dimension, but provides no base effect atom for establishing the initial attack count. A new effect atom is needed: modify_attack_count, carrying an attacksPerAttackAction count (expressed as ThresholdTiers<number> with axis=class to capture the fighter's L5→L11→L20 progression).","evidence":"You can attack twice instead of once whenever you take the Attack action on your turn."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"scale_attack_count (v4 atom not yet implemented in surface)","justification":"The v4 taxonomy explicitly defines scale_attack_count as a scaling atom for 'the number of attacks per Attack action grows with level — Extra Attack (2→4), Fighter Two Extra Attacks / Three Extra Attacks'. This atom exists in v4 but is absent from types.ts and tracer.ts. It is the scaling companion to modify_attack_count: the base modify_attack_count effect sets 2 attacks at L5; scale_attack_count nodes (modifies edges) express the L11→3 and L20→4 progressions.","evidence":"You can attack twice instead of once whenever you take the Attack action on your turn."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3977097-fighter_extra_attack/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:1180\n      throw new Error(`unhandled class-feature family: ${String(_exhaustive)}`);\n            ^\n\n\nError: unhandled class-feature family: passive_modifier\n    at traceClassFeatureMechanics (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3977097-fighter_extra_attack/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:1180:13)\n    at traceClassFeatureUnit (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3977097-fighter_extra_attack/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:1152:23)\n    at traceUnit (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3977097-fighter_extra_attack/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:85:14)\n    at main (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3977097-fighter_extra_attack/src/run.ts:31:17)\n    at <anonymous> (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/3977097-fighter_extra_attack/src/run.ts:49:1)\n    at ModuleJob.run (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:325:25)\n    at async ModuleLoader.import (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:606:24)\n    at async asyncRunEntryPointWithESMLoader (node:internal/modules/run_main:117:5)\n\nNode.js v20.20.1\n","wall_seconds":1.715}

{"unit_slug":"monk_martial_arts","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["activate","bonus_action_quota","class_feature_root","grant_extra_action","rest_window","use_count"],"harness_relations":["consumes","grants","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"passive_bundle family for ClassFeatureMechanics","justification":"Martial Arts is not an activation — it is a passive, always-on set of three conditional benefits that apply whenever the monk meets an equipment precondition (unarmed or monk weapons only, no armor, no shield). The current surface only supports ClassFeatureActivationMechanics (family: 'activation'), which models a discrete use-count trigger with a single effect. A new 'passive_bundle' family is needed to carry an equipment precondition and a list of passive sub-effects that fire unconditionally while the condition holds.","evidence":"You gain the following benefits while you are unarmed or wielding only Monk weapons and you aren't wearing armor or wielding a Shield."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"equipment_precondition","justification":"The three Martial Arts benefits are gated on an equipment state: (a) unarmed or wielding only Monk weapons, (b) not wearing armor, (c) not wielding a Shield. No precondition atom exists in the current surface. A new atom is needed to model 'benefits are suppressed when this equipment gate is not met'.","evidence":"while you are unarmed or wielding only Monk weapons and you aren't wearing armor or wielding a Shield"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"grant_unarmed_attack (ClassFeatureEffect variant)","justification":"Bonus Unarmed Strike grants the specific right to make one Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action — not a free full-action choice. The existing grant_extra_action gives an unrestricted extra action, and there is no way to constrain it to a single attack type. A dedicated effect atom is needed: { kind: 'grant_unarmed_attack', cost: 'bonus_action' }. The per-turn cadence also has no reset analogue in RestResetCadence (closest wrong fit is short_or_long_rest).","evidence":"You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"alt_damage_die (ClassFeatureEffect variant)","justification":"Martial Arts Die lets the monk substitute the weapon's normal damage die with a scaling die (1d6 → 1d8 → 1d10 → 1d12 by class level). This is a die-override/substitution on a weapon's own damage roll, not an additional damage effect. No existing atom in ClassFeatureEffect covers die substitution. The DiceAmount type supports threshold_tiers scaling, but there is no 'override weapon damage die' effect carrier. Proposed: { kind: 'alt_damage_die'; appliesTo: WeaponFilter; scaling: DiceAmount } where WeaponFilter distinguishes 'unarmed_strike' from 'monk_weapon'.","evidence":"You can roll 1d6 in place of the normal damage of your Unarmed Strike or Monk weapons. This die changes as you gain Monk levels, as shown in the Martial Arts column of the Monk Features table."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"ability_mod_substitute (ClassFeatureEffect variant)","justification":"Dexterous Attacks lets the monk use DEX instead of STR for attack rolls, damage rolls, and Grapple/Shove save DCs with Unarmed Strikes and Monk weapons. There is no ability-modifier substitution atom anywhere in the surface. The existing roll_modifier (DiceDelta) adds a fixed die delta to a roll — it cannot swap which ability modifier is applied. A new atom is needed: { kind: 'ability_mod_substitute'; swapFrom: Ability; swapTo: Ability; on: RollKind[]; weaponFilter: WeaponFilter }.","evidence":"You can use your Dexterity modifier instead of your Strength modifier for the attack and damage rolls of your Unarmed Strikes and Monk weapons. In addition, when you use the Grapple or Shove option of your Unarmed Strike, you can use your Dexterity modifier instead of your Strength modifier to determine the save DC."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"RestResetCadence.per_turn (or 'unlimited')","justification":"Bonus Unarmed Strike has no per-rest limit — the monk can use it every turn as long as the equipment precondition is met. The current RestResetCadence variants (short_or_long_rest, long_rest, short_rest, partial_short_full_long) all describe rest-based refills of a depleting pool. Bonus Unarmed Strike is not a pool at all. A new variant — { kind: 'per_turn' } or simply removing the resource/resetCadence requirement from certain activation shapes — is needed.","evidence":"You can make an Unarmed Strike as a Bonus Action. [No restriction on number of uses per rest.]"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.724}

