{"unit_slug":"mastery_sap","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["attack_roll","mastery_root","modify_roll_advantage","on_hit_window","target","turn_start_window"],"harness_relations":["attaches_to","grants","opens_window","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"atom_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_variant","name":"UseCountCap.ability_score_modifier","justification":"The use count is equal to the caster's Charisma modifier with a minimum of 1. Neither 'fixed' (a static integer) nor 'threshold_tiers' (class-level thresholds) can express an ability-score-derived pool. A new variant is needed: { kind: 'ability_score_modifier'; ability: Ability; minimum: number }.","evidence":"You can confer a Bardic Inspiration die a number of times equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of once)"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"grant_buff_die_to_target","justification":"The core effect of Bardic Inspiration is granting a die token to another creature. The target holds the die (up to 1 hour) and may expend it reactively when they fail a D20 Test, adding the die roll to the d20. This reactive, target-held, expend-on-fail pattern is absent from ClassFeatureEffect. The required atom must carry: (a) a DiceAmount expressing the die size with class-level scaling (d6 → d8@L5 → d10@L10 → d12@L15 via threshold_tiers on axis=class); (b) a trigger window (target fails D20 Test); (c) a persist duration (1 hour); (d) single-use-per-holder semantics (die is expended on roll). The existing heal_hp and grant_extra_action effects model neither reactive-hold nor die-token patterns.","evidence":"That creature gains one of your Bardic Inspiration dice. Once within the next hour when the creature fails a D20 Test, the creature can roll the Bardic Inspiration die and add the number rolled to the d20, potentially turning the failure into a success. A Bardic Inspiration die is expended when it's rolled."},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"ClassFeature outbound attachment (range + perceptibility)","justification":"ClassFeatureMechanicsHeader has no attachment or range field. Bardic Inspiration requires targeting another creature within 60 feet who can see or hear the bard — neither the range nor the perceptibility gate can be expressed anywhere in the current class-feature payload. The heal_hp effect has a rudimentary target: 'self' | 'target_creature' but carries no range or sensory constraint. A proper class-feature attachment concept is needed (at minimum range + a visibility/audibility predicate).","evidence":"you can inspire another creature within 60 feet of yourself who can see or hear you"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["claude claimed atom 'activate' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'bonus_action_quota' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'class_feature_root' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'grant_extra_action' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'rest_window' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'use_count' not in tracer output","tracer emitted atom 'attack_roll' not in claude's claim","tracer emitted atom 'mastery_root' not in claude's claim","tracer emitted atom 'modify_roll_advantage' not in claude's claim","tracer emitted atom 'on_hit_window' not in claude's claim","tracer emitted atom 'target' not in claude's claim","tracer emitted atom 'turn_start_window' not in claude's claim"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.665}

