{"unit_slug":"animate_objects","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["action_quota","activate","concentrate","concentration_lock","damage","expire","on_hit_window","scale_die_count","scale_target_count","spell_root","spell_slot","target"],"harness_relations":["attaches_to","consumes","grants","modifies","opens_window","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"atom_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_atom","name":"summon_construct","justification":"The core mechanic of Animate Objects is creature summoning: nonmagical objects transform into Animated Object constructs that act autonomously under the caster's control. The existing OngoingOperation variants (roll_modifier, damage_on_hit) cannot represent this — they model modifications to existing creatures or the caster's own attacks, not the creation of independently-acting combatants. The encoding is forced to use damage_on_hit as a distorted placeholder, which the tracer interprets as 'caster deals bonus damage on hit' — semantically wrong. A new summon_construct operation variant is needed for ongoing_effect mechanics that spawn creatures.","evidence":"Each target animates, sprouts legs, and becomes a Construct that uses the Animated Object stat block; this creature is under your control until the spell ends or until it is reduced to 0 Hit Points."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"TargetSelection.ability_mod_scaled","justification":"The number of objects the caster can animate equals their spellcasting ability modifier, with size weighting (Medium/smaller counts as 1, Large as 2, Huge as 3). The current TargetSelection type only supports mode: 'choose_up_to' with SlotScaling<number> — slot-level-driven count. No ability-modifier scaling variant exists. The encoding uses a hardcoded base: 4 (a +4 modifier guess) with perSlotAboveBase: 0, silently erasing the ability-score dependency. Note: the tracer still emits a scale_target_count node for this because the condition checks for 'choose_up_to + linear' regardless of whether perSlotAboveBase is zero.","evidence":"The maximum number of objects is equal to your spellcasting ability modifier; for this number, a Medium or smaller target counts as one object, a Large target counts as two, and a Huge target counts as three."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"per_size_damage_track","justification":"Animate Objects' Slam attack deals damage that varies by target size (bludgeoning for Medium/smaller, piercing for Large, slashing for Huge) with different upcast scaling per size category (+1d4/+1d6/+1d12 respectively per slot above 5). The current DiceAmount type supports a single damage track and DamageEffect has a single damageType. There is no variant for size-partitioned damage. This widening is best expressed as a sub-structure inside the proposed summon_construct operation, but is documented separately because it requires extending the damage model independently.","evidence":"The creature's Slam damage increases by 1d4 (Medium or smaller), 1d6 (Large), or 1d12 (Huge) for each spell slot level above 5."},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"command_window","justification":"While the spell is active, the caster can spend a Bonus Action each round to mentally command any or all summoned creatures within 500 feet simultaneously, issuing the same command to multiple at once. This is a recurring optional bonus-action window on the ongoing effect that re-opens each turn. It is distinct from a one-time bonus action (like mark_transfer): it persists for the spell duration, not triggered by a single event. No existing atom — window or operation — captures a recurring per-turn optional command dispatch linked to summoned creatures.","evidence":"Until the spell ends, you can take a Bonus Action to mentally command any creature you made with this spell if the creature is within 500 feet of you (if you control multiple creatures, you can command any of them at the same time, issuing the same command to each one)."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":2.389}

{"unit_slug":"antimagic_field","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":1,"harness_atoms":[],"harness_relations":[],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"atom_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_variant","name":"AreaOrigin.emanation","justification":"Antimagic Field has range 'Self' and creates a 10-foot Emanation — an area that moves with the caster for the spell's duration. The surface's AreaOrigin only has 'point_within_range' (fixed point in space) and 'on_primary_target'. Neither captures a sphere bound to and repositioning with the caster. This is a surface widening of an existing v4 'area' attachment atom; no new v4 atom is required.","evidence":"An aura of antimagic surrounds you in a 10-foot Emanation. (SRD: 'An emanation spell has a range of Self and creates an area of effect that extends outward from you... The effect moves with you.')"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"OngoingOperation.suppress_magic_zone","justification":"The surface's OngoingOperation is a closed union of roll_modifier | damage_on_hit. Antimagic Field's core mechanic is total magic suppression in the attachment area: no spellcasting, no Magic actions, no magic item properties, no targeting in/out, ongoing spells suppressed. The v4 taxonomy has 'suppress' (procedure) and 'block_targeting' (effect) but neither is wired into OngoingOperation. The tracer threw 'unhandled ongoing operation' at tracer.ts:509 confirming this is a blocking gap. A new suppress_magic_zone variant (or a new zone_suppression spell family) is required.","evidence":"No one can cast spells, take Magic actions, or create other magical effects inside the aura... Magical properties of magic items don't work inside the aura or on anything inside it. Ongoing spells... are suppressed in the area. While an effect is suppressed, it doesn't function, but the time it spends suppressed counts against its duration."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":["claude claimed atom 'action_quota' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'activate' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'area' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'concentrate' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'concentration_lock' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'expire' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'spell_root' not in tracer output","claude claimed atom 'spell_slot' not in tracer output"],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/191480-antimagic_field/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:509\n      throw new Error(`unhandled ongoing operation: ${String(_)}`);\n            ^\n\n\nError: unhandled ongoing operation: [object Object]\n    at traceOngoingOperation (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/191480-antimagic_field/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:509:13)\n    at traceOngoingEffect (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/191480-antimagic_field/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:382:3)\n    at traceSpellMechanics (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/191480-antimagic_field/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:163:7)\n    at traceSpellUnit (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/191480-antimagic_field/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:118:23)\n    at traceUnit (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/191480-antimagic_field/src/interpreter/tracer.ts:83:14)\n    at main (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/191480-antimagic_field/src/run.ts:31:17)\n    at <anonymous> (/workspace/typescript/dnd/scripts/content-surface-survey/workers/191480-antimagic_field/src/run.ts:49:1)\n    at ModuleJob.run (node:internal/modules/esm/module_job:325:25)\n    at async ModuleLoader.import (node:internal/modules/esm/loader:606:24)\n    at async asyncRunEntryPointWithESMLoader (node:internal/modules/run_main:117:5)\n\nNode.js v20.20.1\n","wall_seconds":1.435}

