{"unit_slug":"banishment","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["action_quota","activate","concentrate","concentration_lock","expire","save_gate","scale_target_count","spell_root","spell_slot","target"],"harness_relations":["attaches_to","consumes","grants","modifies","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"atom_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_variant","name":"Effect.apply_condition","justification":"Banishment's on-fail branch applies the Incapacitated condition to the target. The Effect type for spell activation phases is currently `DamageEffect | NoneEffect`. There is no variant for applying a condition. The mastery layer has an `apply_condition` result for SaveGateRider, but it is not surfaced as a spell Effect. Without this variant, the save_gate phase branches can only express damage or nothing — the actual on-fail outcome (condition application) cannot be encoded.","evidence":"\"the target has the Incapacitated condition\""},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"Condition.incapacitated","justification":"Even if Effect.apply_condition is added, the Condition type only contains \"prone\" (used by Topple mastery). Banishment requires \"incapacitated\". The Condition type must be widened to include all SRD conditions that spells can apply.","evidence":"\"the target has the Incapacitated condition\""},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"remove_from_play","justification":"Banishment's core mechanic is removing the target from the battlefield entirely — they are transported to a harmless demiplane and cannot participate in combat for the duration. This is not a condition, not damage, and not a movement effect. v4 has no atom for 'remove creature from the active plane temporarily'. Without this atom, the save_gate on-fail branch can only gesture at the incapacitation rider; the battlefield removal (which is the primary tactical effect of Banishment) is entirely unrepresentable.","evidence":"\"be transported to a harmless demiplane for the duration\""},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"conditional_on_duration_expiry","justification":"If the spell lasts its full 1-minute duration AND the target is a planar creature type (Aberration, Celestial, Elemental, Fey, Fiend), the banishment becomes permanent — the creature is sent to a random location on its home plane and never returns. This is an end-of-concentration conditional: 'if concentration held to natural expiry AND condition predicate on target type, then apply permanent effect'. The surface has no lifecycle atom or relation for this pattern. The `expire` atom marks when concentration ends but has no hook for conditional effects at that moment.","evidence":"\"If the target is an Aberration, a Celestial, an Elemental, a Fey, or a Fiend, the target doesn't return if the spell lasts for 1 minute.\""}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.345}

