{"unit_slug":"bestow_curse","verdict":"structural_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["action_quota","activate","concentrate","concentration_lock","damage","expire","on_hit_window","spell_root","spell_slot","target"],"harness_relations":["attaches_to","consumes","grants","opens_window","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"structural_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"save_gate_then_ongoing_effect","justification":"Bestow Curse requires an initial Wisdom saving throw at cast time; on failure, the curse (an ongoing concentration effect) is applied for the duration. No existing family models this composition: ongoing_effect attaches directly with no save gate, and activation's Effect type (damage | none) has no ongoing-application output. A new payload family — or a hybrid composition where activation can hand off to ongoing_effect on a specified branch — is needed.","evidence":"You touch a creature, which must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or become cursed for the duration."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"OngoingOperation.modify_roll_advantage","justification":"Options A and B impose Disadvantage as a persistent ongoing effect. Option A: Disadvantage on all ability checks and saving throws using one chosen ability. Option B: Disadvantage on the target's attack rolls against the caster. The v4 atom modify_roll_advantage exists and is wired into the mastery surface (ModifyRollAdvantageRider) but is absent from spell OngoingOperation. A new variant of OngoingOperation is needed, analogous to how modify_roll_numeric is already an OngoingOperation variant.","evidence":"Choose one ability. The target has Disadvantage on ability checks and saving throws made with that ability. / The target has Disadvantage on attack rolls against you."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"OngoingOperation.repeat_save_forced_action","justification":"Option C fires at the start of each of the target's turns: the target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or be forced to take the Dodge action on that turn. This requires a repeat_save resolution (v4 atom exists but is not wired into the surface) triggered by a turn_start_window, with a restrict_action_set effect on failure. There is no OngoingOperation variant that opens a per-turn resolution window with a conditional action-forcing effect.","evidence":"In combat, the target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw at the start of each of its turns or be forced to take the Dodge action on that turn."},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"SpellMechanics.choose_one_operation","justification":"The caster chooses one of 4 distinct curse effects at cast time. The v4 taxonomy has a choose procedure atom, but the surface has no dispatch mechanism for caster-at-cast-time option selection among multiple OngoingOperation variants. All four option branches need to be representable so that the harness can prompt the caster for their choice and apply the selected operation for the spell's duration.","evidence":"Until the curse ends, the target suffers one of the following effects of your choice."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.502}

{"unit_slug":"befuddlement","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["action_quota","activate","damage","save_gate","spell_root","spell_slot","target"],"harness_relations":["attaches_to","branches_on_save","consumes","grants","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"atom_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_atom","name":"apply_restriction","justification":"Befuddlement's on-fail branch imposes a persistent action suppression: target can't cast spells or take the Magic action. Effect = DamageEffect | NoneEffect has no variant for action suppression. This is a distinct effect from damage — it survives long after the instantaneous cast and governs the target's action economy on every subsequent turn.","evidence":"the target takes 10d12 Psychic damage and can't cast spells or take the Magic action"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"compound_effect (or Effect as array)","justification":"The on-fail branch simultaneously applies TWO independent effects: 10d12 Psychic damage and an action restriction. Effect is a single discriminated union; there is no way to express 'damage AND restriction' on one save branch without a compound/multi-effect wrapper. Either Effect must become ReadonlyArray<SingleEffect> or a new CompoundEffect variant must be added.","evidence":"the target takes 10d12 Psychic damage and can't cast spells or take the Magic action"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"indefinite_periodic_save","justification":"The action restriction has no fixed duration. It persists indefinitely until the target succeeds on a repeated saving throw made at 30-day intervals. Current Duration models are: instantaneous (no state), concentration (caster-maintained, rounds-to-minutes), and timed (fixed calendar value). None captures 'indefinitely, with periodic save opportunities every 30 days'.","evidence":"At the end of every 30 days, the target repeats the save, ending the effect on a success"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"spell_cure_condition","justification":"The action restriction can be ended by casting specific named spells on the target (Greater Restoration, Heal, Wish). No existing lifecycle atom models 'effect ends when one of these named spells is cast on the target'. This is distinct from concentration-break and timed expiry.","evidence":"The effect can also be ended by the Greater Restoration, Heal, or Wish spell"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.31}

{"unit_slug":"bless","verdict":"atom_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["action_quota","activate","concentrate","concentration_lock","expire","modify_roll_numeric","scale_target_count","spell_root","spell_slot","target"],"harness_relations":["attaches_to","consumes","grants","modifies","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"atom_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_atom","name":"grant_advantage_on_save","justification":"Beacon of Hope grants Advantage on Wisdom saving throws and on Death Saving Throws for the duration of concentration. OngoingOperation only has roll_modifier (numeric die delta) and damage_on_hit — neither can express advantage. The mastery-context ModifyRollAdvantageRider is structurally similar but carries count and expiresOn fields that are mastery-specific. A new OngoingOperation variant is needed: { kind: 'grant_advantage'; abilityFilter?: Ability; includesDeathSaves?: boolean } to distinguish Wisdom-scoped saves from all saves.","evidence":"each target has Advantage on Wisdom saving throws and Death Saving Throws"},{"kind":"new_atom","name":"maximize_healing_received","justification":"Beacon of Hope forces every healing roll to its maximum value for affected targets. There is no atom or operation in the surface that represents modifying incoming healing calculations. HealHpEffect exists but models the caster dealing healing, not a buff that intercepts healing received by a target from any source. A new OngoingOperation variant is needed: { kind: 'maximize_healing' } with no additional parameters.","evidence":"regains the maximum number of Hit Points possible from any healing"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"OngoingEffectMechanics.operations (array)","justification":"OngoingEffectMechanics has a single 'operation' field. Beacon of Hope requires two concurrent ongoing operations (grant_advantage_on_save + maximize_healing_received) on the same attachment. The field must become 'operations: ReadonlyArray<OngoingOperation>' to support multiple simultaneous effects. The proxy encoding silently drops maximize_healing_received entirely.","evidence":"each target has Advantage on Wisdom saving throws and Death Saving Throws and regains the maximum number of Hit Points possible from any healing"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"TargetSelection.any_number","justification":"Beacon of Hope targets 'any number of creatures within range' — an unbounded, player-chosen subset with no numeric cap and no slot-scaling. TargetSelection only offers { mode: 'one' } or { mode: 'choose_up_to'; count: SlotScaling<number> }. A new variant { mode: 'any_number' } (no count field) is needed. The proxy encoding uses choose_up_to with base 99, which is semantically wrong.","evidence":"Choose any number of creatures within range"}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.371}

