{"unit_slug":"blindness_deafness","verdict":"surface_widening","typecheck_exit":0,"tracer_exit":0,"harness_atoms":["action_quota","activate","expire","persist","save_gate","scale_target_count","spell_root","spell_slot","target"],"harness_relations":["attaches_to","consumes","grants","modifies","persists_until","roots"],"unknown_atoms":[],"unknown_relations":[],"claude_self_verdict":"surface_widening","claude_proposed_widenings":[{"kind":"new_variant","name":"Effect.apply_condition","justification":"The spell's core mechanic is applying Blinded or Deafened on a failed CON save. ActivationPhase.onFail is typed as Effect = DamageEffect | NoneEffect — there is no apply_condition variant. The apply_condition atomKind already exists in v4 (mastery tracer traceSaveGateResult) but is inaccessible from spell Effect. Encoding was forced to onFail: {kind:\"none\"}, dropping the spell's entire payoff.","evidence":"it has the Blinded or Deafened condition (your choice) for the duration"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"Condition: blinded and deafened","justification":"The Condition type currently only contains \"prone\". Blindness/Deafness requires \"blinded\" and \"deafened\" as valid Condition discriminants. Even after adding the apply_condition Effect variant, both conditions are unrepresentable without widening the Condition union.","evidence":"it has the Blinded or Deafened condition (your choice) for the duration"},{"kind":"new_variant","name":"Effect.apply_condition_choice (caster-elected condition)","justification":"The caster selects which condition to apply at cast time. A single apply_condition can't express this — it needs a ChoiceEffect wrapper or a dedicated variant such as { kind: \"apply_condition_choice\"; options: ReadonlyArray<Condition> }. No caster-election mechanism exists in any current Effect variant.","evidence":"the Blinded or Deafened condition (your choice)"},{"kind":"new_subgraph","name":"timed_repeating_save_to_end","justification":"At the end of each of the target's turns it repeats the CON save; success ends the spell early. The atoms required (turn_end_window, save_gate, expire) all exist in v4, but no surface type wires them for timed spells. This repeating-save termination pattern recurs across Hold Person, Slow, and similar debuff spells. Needs either a new ActivationPhase kind or a repeatingSave field on the timed Duration variant.","evidence":"At the end of each of its turns, the target repeats the save, ending the spell on itself on a success."}],"claude_confidence":"high","discrepancies":[],"typecheck_stderr":"","tracer_stderr":"","wall_seconds":1.381}

